# API Client Rules — Venue Connectors

## Kalshi Public API
- Base URL: https://trading-api.kalshi.com/trade-api/v2
- Authentication: None required for public market data
- Key endpoints:
  - GET /markets — list markets with optional search
  - GET /markets/{ticker} — single market by ticker
- Rate limiting: Be respectful, add delays if needed

## Polymarket Public API
- Base URL: https://gamma-api.polymarket.com
- Authentication: None required for public market data
- Key endpoints:
  - GET /markets — list markets with optional search/filter
  - GET /markets/{id} — single market by ID
- Note: Polymarket also has a CLOB API at clob.polymarket.com for order book data

## HTTP Client Rules
Every venue client must:

```go
// 1. Use a shared HTTP client with timeout (not http.DefaultClient)
type KalshiClient struct {
    httpClient *http.Client
    baseURL    string
    logger     *logger.Logger
}

func NewKalshiClient(cfg *config.Config, log *logger.Logger) *KalshiClient {
    return &KalshiClient{
        httpClient: &http.Client{
            Timeout: cfg.HTTPTimeout, // from config, default 10s
        },
        baseURL: cfg.KalshiBaseURL,
        logger:  log,
    }
}

// 2. Always use context
req, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, url, nil)

// 3. Always set Accept header
req.Header.Set("Accept", "application/json")

// 4. Always check status code
if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {
    return nil, &equinoxerrors.EquinoxError{
        Layer:   "connector",
        Venue:   "kalshi",
        Message: fmt.Sprintf("API returned status %d", resp.StatusCode),
    }
}

// 5. Always close body
defer resp.Body.Close()

// 6. Always decode into raw struct first
var raw KalshiResponse
if err := json.NewDecoder(resp.Body).Decode(&raw); err != nil {
    return nil, &equinoxerrors.EquinoxError{
        Layer:   "connector",
        Venue:   "kalshi",
        Message: "failed to decode response",
        Err:     err,
    }
}
```

## Query Building
Build URLs cleanly using url.Values:

```go
params := url.Values{}
params.Set("limit", "50")
if query != "" {
    params.Set("search", query)
}
fullURL := fmt.Sprintf("%s/markets?%s", c.baseURL, params.Encode())
```

## Logging in Connectors
Log at key points:

```go
// Before fetch
c.logger.Info("connector", "kalshi", fmt.Sprintf("fetching markets for query: %s", query))

// After successful fetch
c.logger.Info("connector", "kalshi", fmt.Sprintf("fetched %d markets", len(markets)))

// On warn (partial data)
c.logger.Warn("connector", "kalshi", "market missing liquidity data, defaulting to 0")

// On error (before returning)
c.logger.Error("connector", "kalshi", "fetch failed", err)
```

## Adapter Rules
The adapter transforms raw venue structs into canonical Market structs.
Adapters live in venues/kalshi/adapter.go and venues/polymarket/adapter.go.

```go
// Adapter function signature — always this pattern
func AdaptKalshiMarket(raw KalshiMarket) (models.Market, error) {
    // 1. Parse dates
    resolvesAt, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339, raw.CloseTime)
    if err != nil {
        return models.Market{}, &equinoxerrors.EquinoxError{
            Layer:   "normalizer",
            Venue:   "kalshi",
            Message: fmt.Sprintf("failed to parse close_time: %s", raw.CloseTime),
            Err:     err,
        }
    }

    // 2. Validate prices
    if raw.YesBid < 0 || raw.YesBid > 1 || raw.YesAsk < 0 || raw.YesAsk > 1 {
        return models.Market{}, &equinoxerrors.EquinoxError{
            Layer:   "normalizer",
            Venue:   "kalshi",
            Message: fmt.Sprintf("invalid price range: bid=%f ask=%f", raw.YesBid, raw.YesAsk),
        }
    }

    // 3. Build canonical market
    mid := (raw.YesBid + raw.YesAsk) / 2
    return models.Market{
        ID:         generateID(raw.Ticker),
        VenueID:    raw.Ticker,
        Venue:      "kalshi",
        Title:      normalizeTitle(raw.Title),
        YesBid:     raw.YesBid,
        YesAsk:     raw.YesAsk,
        YesMid:     mid,
        NoPrice:    1.0 - mid,
        Spread:     raw.YesAsk - raw.YesBid,
        Liquidity:  raw.Liquidity,
        Volume24h:  raw.Volume24h,
        ResolvesAt: resolvesAt,
        FetchedAt:  time.Now(),
        Category:   raw.Category,
        Status:     raw.Status,
        RawData:    raw,
    }, nil
}
```

## Title Normalization
Always normalize titles for equivalence comparison:

```go
func normalizeTitle(title string) string {
    // lowercase
    title = strings.ToLower(title)
    // remove punctuation
    title = regexp.MustCompile(`[^\w\s]`).ReplaceAllString(title, "")
    // collapse whitespace
    title = strings.Join(strings.Fields(title), " ")
    // trim
    return strings.TrimSpace(title)
}
```
